            "normalized_html": "<p>Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u222b_{1}^{2}(1)/(x^{3})dx|= \u222b_{1}^{2}x^{\u2212 3}dx; = (x^{\u2212 3 + 1})/(\u2212 3 + 1)|_{1}^{2}; = \u2212 (x^{\u2212 2})/(2)|_{1}^{2}; = \u2212 (1)/(2)(2^{\u2212 2} \u2212 1^{\u2212 2}); = \u2212 (1)/(2)((1)/(4) \u2212 1); = \u2212 (1)/(2)(\u2212 (3)/(4)); = (3)/(8).]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n[MATH: \u222b_{1}^{2}(1)/(x^{3})dx|= \u222b_{1}^{2}x^{\u2212 3}dx; = (x^{\u2212 3 + 1})/(\u2212 3 + 1)|_{1}^{2}; = \u2212 (x^{\u2212 2})/(2)|_{1}^{2}; = \u2212 (1)/(2)(2^{\u2212 2} \u2212 1^{\u2212 2}); = \u2212 (1)/(2)((1)/(4) \u2212 1); = \u2212 (1)/(2)(\u2212 (3)/(4)); = (3)/(8).]",
